msgid "Synchronisation is paused: {reason}"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:730
msgid "End-to-end encryption"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:733
msgid ""
"Encryption is unavailable because the 'cryptography' package is missing. "
"Synchronisation itself is unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:746
msgid ""
"On for everything from now on. What was synchronised before is still on the "
"server in plain text: it goes as soon as this device has sent an encrypted "
"summary, which happens by itself on one of the next few syncs."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:751
msgid "On. The server stores only ciphertext it cannot read."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:752
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Key fingerprint: {fingerprint}"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:754
msgid ""
"This must read the same on every device of this account, unless the "
"passphrase has just been changed on one of them."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:765
msgid ""
"Sign in above first. Encryption is tied to the account, so it cannot be set "
"up before this device knows which one it is."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:770
msgid ""
"Encryption is switched on for this account, but the settings carry no salt "
"to derive the key from. Copy config.json from the device that has it, or "
"switch encryption off and on again to start over - which makes the data "
"already on the server unreadable."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:779
msgid ""
"On for this account, but this device does not have the key yet. Nothing is "
"being synchronised until you enter the passphrase."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:783
msgid ""
"The key stored here does not belong to these settings - the salt or the "
"account has changed since it was made. Enter the passphrase again."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:787 sl/SL_Menu.py:839
msgid "Passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:789
msgid "Unlock this device"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:791
msgid "Please enter the passphrase."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:793 sl/SL_Menu.py:857 sl/SL_Menu.py:895
msgid "Deriving the key..."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:800
msgid "Key stored. Check that the fingerprint matches your other device."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:812
msgid ""
"Off. This account has been encrypted before, so switching it back on uses "
"the same passphrase as then - nothing is asked for again. What is on the "
"server from the meantime was sent unencrypted."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:816
msgid "Switch encryption back on"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:821
msgid "Encryption is on again."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:823
msgid ""
"Encryption is on again. This device no longer has the key - enter the "
"passphrase."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:832
msgid ""
"Project and task names, notes and times are stored on the sync server in "
"plain text. Switching this on seals them on this device first, so the server "
"only ever holds ciphertext."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:835
msgid ""
"The passphrase is not your account password, and it is never sent to the "
"server. Nobody can recover it for you: if it is lost, so is everything the "
"server holds."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:840
msgid "Repeat the passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:842
msgid ""
"Update your other devices and the sync server first. An older version does "
"not recognise encrypted data: the server refuses it outright, and an older "
"device would quietly stop receiving anything."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:846
msgid ""
"Your other devices then need this same passphrase, and the config.json from "
"this one - it carries the salt."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:848
msgid "Switch encryption on"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:850 tt/sync_messages.py:146
msgid "Please enter a passphrase."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:855 sl/SL_Menu.py:928
msgid "The two passphrases are not the same."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:861
msgid ""
"Encryption is on. Write the passphrase down somewhere safe - it cannot be "
"recovered."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:889 sl/SL_Menu.py:920
msgid "New passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:891
msgid "Add this passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:899
msgid ""
"Key added. The older one is kept, so what was synchronised before stays "
"readable."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:915
msgid "Change the passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:916
msgid ""
"The new one has to reach your other devices as well. Until it does, they "
"stop synchronising and say so - nothing is lost, and the old passphrase is "
"not needed again."
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:922
msgid "Repeat the new passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:924
msgid "Change it"
msgstr ""

#: sl/SL_Menu.py:930
msgid "Sealing everything with the new key..."
